To give you some good news (perhaps :-)

all \text.. comannds as well as \emph in LaTeX2e will do
proper italic correction on both sides of the command and
will in addition have a customisable list of chars (not a fixed set).

However, it is not completely trivial to produce this result and a blind
use of \futurelet is a timebomb as you will find out after a while.

consider a part of fancyheadings.sty that says

....\leftmark\fi ...

now if you get \emph{foo} into that mark it will future let to \fi
with interesting consequences ...

anyway wait and see it is coming

cheers Frank

